1
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:41,017
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:45,017
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,017 --> 00:02:52,017
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,017 --> 00:02:58,017
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:58,017 --> 00:03:09,017
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,017 --> 00:03:13,017
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:16,017 --> 00:03:23,017
The first stop on Luffy's journey is Fishman Island, thousands of feet below sea level, where his crew becomes involved in a civil war.

8
00:03:23,017 --> 00:03:28,017
Jinbei tells them the tragic history of the island and reveals his connection to Arlong.

9
00:03:28,017 --> 00:03:32,017
Despite his role in Nami's suffering, she forgives him wholeheartedly.

10
00:03:32,017 --> 00:03:36,017
Soon after, the Straw Hats receive a surprise transmission.

11
00:03:36,017 --> 00:03:42,017
Hello there, people of Fishman Island. Am I coming through?

12
00:03:42,017 --> 00:03:51,017
Well then, for those of you who don't know, I'm the captain of the new Fishman Pirates.

13
00:03:51,017 --> 00:03:55,017
My name is Horty Jones!

14
00:03:59,017 --> 00:04:04,017
The Kingdom in Shock, an order to execute Neptune issued.

15
00:04:04,017 --> 00:04:07,017
Come on! Next!

16
00:04:07,017 --> 00:04:08,017
Next!

17
00:04:08,017 --> 00:04:09,017
Next!

18
00:04:13,017 --> 00:04:14,017
Next!

19
00:04:20,017 --> 00:04:21,017
You won't step on it?

20
00:04:21,017 --> 00:04:27,017
I'm sure Queen Otohime would forgive us.

21
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:30,017
If I refuse, they'll kill me.

22
00:04:30,017 --> 00:04:32,017
I can't believe this is happening.

23
00:04:32,017 --> 00:04:33,017
I'm sorry, Queen Otohime.

24
00:04:33,017 --> 00:04:35,017
I don't want to.

25
00:04:35,017 --> 00:04:36,017
There you go.

26
00:04:36,017 --> 00:04:37,017
Next!

27
00:04:40,017 --> 00:04:41,017
Kya-kya!

28
00:04:41,017 --> 00:04:42,017
How boring!

29
00:04:42,017 --> 00:04:44,017
No one's even trying to resist!

30
00:04:44,017 --> 00:04:45,017
Ha!

31
00:04:45,017 --> 00:04:48,017
People are stomping on her without a second thought!

32
00:04:48,017 --> 00:04:49,017
Kya-kya!

33
00:04:49,017 --> 00:04:50,017
Hey Daruma!

34
00:04:50,017 --> 00:04:51,017
You gotta come see this quick!

35
00:04:51,017 --> 00:04:53,017
Captain Horty's live on the air!

36
00:04:53,017 --> 00:04:54,017
Huh?

37
00:04:58,017 --> 00:05:00,017
So he's the one behind all this.

38
00:05:00,017 --> 00:05:01,017
The bastard!

39
00:05:01,017 --> 00:05:03,017
Why does he want us to stuff on the Queen so bad?

40
00:05:03,017 --> 00:05:04,017
Wait!

41
00:05:04,017 --> 00:05:05,017
That guy?

42
00:05:05,017 --> 00:05:07,017
Wasn't he also the soldier from the plaza?

43
00:05:07,017 --> 00:05:10,017
He killed Otohime's assassin that day!

44
00:05:10,017 --> 00:05:11,017
That's right!

45
00:05:11,017 --> 00:05:12,017
His name is Horty Jones!

46
00:05:12,017 --> 00:05:13,017
The same guy!

47
00:05:13,017 --> 00:05:16,017
Why would one of Neptune's soldiers do such a thing?

48
00:05:16,017 --> 00:05:21,017
There's something every citizen of the Ryugu Kingdom needs to know.

49
00:05:22,017 --> 00:05:24,017
This will be destroyed!

50
00:05:24,017 --> 00:05:25,017
And quickly!

51
00:05:25,017 --> 00:05:27,017
We'll rebuild it from scratch!

52
00:05:27,017 --> 00:05:29,017
But with a new king!

53
00:05:30,017 --> 00:05:31,017
Like me!

54
00:05:43,017 --> 00:05:44,017
What's he talking about?

55
00:05:44,017 --> 00:05:45,017
Who does he think he is?

56
00:05:45,017 --> 00:05:46,017
Screw you!

57
00:05:46,017 --> 00:05:47,017
This is crazy!

58
00:05:47,017 --> 00:05:49,017
Where is this broadcast even coming from?

59
00:05:49,017 --> 00:05:50,017
King Neptune!

60
00:05:50,017 --> 00:05:51,017
Is he okay?

61
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:54,017
The Straw Hat supposedly took over the palace!

62
00:05:54,017 --> 00:05:56,017
Do you think they're his allies?

63
00:05:56,017 --> 00:05:58,017
Nothing makes sense anymore!

64
00:05:58,017 --> 00:06:01,017
I will usher in a new era for Fishman Island!

65
00:06:01,017 --> 00:06:04,017
Grounded in a strict code of discipline!

66
00:06:04,017 --> 00:06:08,017
For starters, we'll end all friendly relations with humans!

67
00:06:08,017 --> 00:06:11,017
So if you like them, get out!

68
00:06:11,017 --> 00:06:12,017
Yes!

69
00:06:12,017 --> 00:06:14,017
Fishmen are far superior to humans!

70
00:06:14,017 --> 00:06:18,017
It's time that race of weaklings learned its place they don't deserve our help!

71
00:06:18,017 --> 00:06:20,017
In place of the sympathizers!

72
00:06:20,017 --> 00:06:24,017
Those loyal to our cause will move in from the Fishman District!

73
00:06:24,017 --> 00:06:26,017
They hate humans too!

74
00:06:26,017 --> 00:06:29,017
And will do whatever it takes to rid this country of them!

75
00:06:29,017 --> 00:06:31,017
So treat them with respect!

76
00:06:31,017 --> 00:06:32,017
Is he serious?

77
00:06:32,017 --> 00:06:33,017
New residents?

78
00:06:33,017 --> 00:06:38,017
He's just gonna let all these criminals roam free through our kingdom?

79
00:06:41,017 --> 00:06:43,017
You still love her, don't you?

80
00:06:43,017 --> 00:06:46,017
Otohime, our most cherished queen!

81
00:06:46,017 --> 00:06:52,017
She was indeed selfless and worked tirelessly to build a bridge between fishmen and humans!

82
00:06:52,017 --> 00:06:54,017
I do respect her spirit!

83
00:06:54,017 --> 00:06:57,017
But have you forgotten the end of her tale?

84
00:06:57,017 --> 00:06:59,017
She was killed by a human!

85
00:06:59,017 --> 00:07:02,017
Even if you approach them with a pure heart and kind intentions,

86
00:07:02,017 --> 00:07:05,017
they'll just take advantage of you and leave you in the dirt!

87
00:07:05,017 --> 00:07:08,017
We have to wake up, can't you see?

88
00:07:08,017 --> 00:07:16,017
Sorry, but the royal family's been duping you for years!

89
00:07:16,017 --> 00:07:19,017
If we follow them, we'll face extinction!

90
00:07:19,017 --> 00:07:23,017
As long as humans exist, this goal of harmony is unattainable!

91
00:07:23,017 --> 00:07:27,017
It's a pipe dream that's been perpetuated for far too long!

92
00:07:27,017 --> 00:07:28,017
Stop it!

93
00:07:28,017 --> 00:07:30,017
See for yourself!

94
00:07:33,017 --> 00:07:34,017
They have father!

95
00:07:34,017 --> 00:07:35,017
How could they?

96
00:07:35,017 --> 00:07:37,017
Father!

97
00:07:37,017 --> 00:07:39,017
Not the king!

98
00:07:39,017 --> 00:07:41,017
King Neptune got old!

99
00:07:41,017 --> 00:07:43,017
It happens to everyone!

100
00:07:44,017 --> 00:07:47,017
The only way to advance is to eliminate the old god,

101
00:07:47,017 --> 00:07:49,017
so they won't hold us back anymore!

102
00:07:52,017 --> 00:07:55,017
Huh, when you think about it, this mess is kind of our fault!

103
00:07:55,017 --> 00:07:57,017
If we hadn't shown up, the king might be fine!

104
00:07:57,017 --> 00:07:58,017
Huh?

105
00:07:58,017 --> 00:08:00,017
More like Zoro's fault!

106
00:08:00,017 --> 00:08:02,017
And that's why you shouldn't feel guilty!

107
00:08:02,017 --> 00:08:06,017
Mosshead just can't keep his swords to himself, that's all!

108
00:08:06,017 --> 00:08:08,017
What in the world did you do at the palace?

109
00:08:08,017 --> 00:08:09,017
Jinbei, wait!

110
00:08:09,017 --> 00:08:10,017
Calm down!

111
00:08:10,017 --> 00:08:13,017
A bunch of Neptune soldiers attacked Namichin and our friends first!

112
00:08:13,017 --> 00:08:15,017
They were just trying to defend themselves!

113
00:08:15,017 --> 00:08:16,017
I'm still confused!

114
00:08:16,017 --> 00:08:17,017
Citizens of Fishman Island!

115
00:08:17,017 --> 00:08:22,017
The old Ryugu Kingdom has worn out its welcome!

116
00:08:22,017 --> 00:08:26,017
Time to say goodbye!

117
00:08:26,017 --> 00:08:36,017
In three hours, at the Conchcord Plaza, the weak and incompetent King Neptune will be put to death!

118
00:08:36,017 --> 00:08:46,017
The Great Pirate Era began when the Navy executed a human, Gold Roger, the king of the pirates!

119
00:08:46,017 --> 00:08:51,017
That era was notable for countless acts of persecution at the hands of humans!

120
00:08:51,017 --> 00:08:58,017
It's only natural then, that Neptune's execution will bring about a great fishman era!

121
00:08:58,017 --> 00:09:02,017
One in between, reign over humans!

122
00:09:02,017 --> 00:09:10,017
As you may have figured out by now, I am at the Ryugu Palace, and there's something else I want to show you!

123
00:09:10,017 --> 00:09:13,017
This here, is from the nobles!

124
00:09:13,017 --> 00:09:15,017
The queen risked her life for this!

125
00:09:15,017 --> 00:09:20,017
Ten years ago, that is!

126
00:09:20,017 --> 00:09:25,017
If I destroy this letter, it's over!

127
00:09:25,017 --> 00:09:26,017
You won't get another one!

128
00:09:26,017 --> 00:09:32,017
Along with that, here we have a box!

129
00:09:32,017 --> 00:09:37,017
With signatures from most of Fishman Island!

130
00:09:37,017 --> 00:09:44,017
Frankly, I'm disgusted by the numbers!

131
00:09:44,017 --> 00:09:49,017
Who in their right mind would want to befriend humans after all they've done?

132
00:09:49,017 --> 00:09:52,017
So, if your name is on any of these, thank you!

133
00:09:52,017 --> 00:09:54,017
I know who I have to weed out!

134
00:09:54,017 --> 00:09:56,017
My kingdom will be better without you!

135
00:09:56,017 --> 00:10:00,017
And with that in mind, why don't we get started?

136
00:10:00,017 --> 00:10:02,017
Here's page one!

137
00:10:02,017 --> 00:10:03,017
Enough stepping on pictures!

138
00:10:03,017 --> 00:10:04,017
That's true!

139
00:10:04,017 --> 00:10:09,017
It's far too easy to pretend you don't mind doing it just to save yourselves!

140
00:10:09,017 --> 00:10:16,017
But these signatures, they give me concrete evidence of who I can suspect will oppose my rule!

141
00:10:16,017 --> 00:10:21,017
It's like you signed your own death warrant!

142
00:10:21,017 --> 00:10:25,017
