230
00:13:35,017 --> 00:14:02,317
Now then, issue an order to Daruma and the others to assemble.

231
00:14:02,877 --> 00:14:04,297
We need to act quickly.

232
00:14:04,297 --> 00:14:05,397
Sure thing, Captain.

233
00:14:06,217 --> 00:14:08,457
Your execution's going to be big.

234
00:14:08,957 --> 00:14:11,097
The more citizens that fear me, the better.

235
00:14:11,717 --> 00:14:15,017
I don't have time to convince everyone that my way is the right one.

236
00:14:15,237 --> 00:14:17,097
You're only thinking of yourself.

237
00:14:17,677 --> 00:14:21,297
Even if you were right, a nation can't prosper in fear.

238
00:14:22,177 --> 00:14:24,817
The truth is, all rulers are selfish.

239
00:14:25,477 --> 00:14:26,497
I'm surprised.

240
00:14:26,837 --> 00:14:29,617
You should know that better than anyone, Your Majesty.

241
00:14:29,617 --> 00:14:35,917
Ever since I was a soldier, I've been dragged along by Queen Otohime's foolish dream.

242
00:14:36,297 --> 00:14:37,237
We all have.

243
00:14:37,657 --> 00:14:39,337
Thankfully, you'll be gone soon.

244
00:14:39,537 --> 00:14:41,377
And then, they'll see the truth.

245
00:14:42,177 --> 00:14:43,077
They'll have to.

246
00:14:43,477 --> 00:14:45,957
Because my law will reign supreme.

247
00:14:45,957 --> 00:14:50,157
Hey, guys.

248
00:14:50,337 --> 00:14:51,837
This water isn't getting any lower.

249
00:14:52,557 --> 00:14:53,137
Oh, no.

250
00:14:53,537 --> 00:14:55,397
I just got dry, too.

251
00:14:55,717 --> 00:14:57,897
Now, let's all figure out a way to save me.

252
00:14:58,697 --> 00:15:00,517
Or better yet, save us.

253
00:15:00,677 --> 00:15:01,997
Do you have any ideas?

254
00:15:02,217 --> 00:15:02,597
Anything?

255
00:15:02,597 --> 00:15:03,717
I'm thinking.

256
00:15:04,297 --> 00:15:07,897
First, get me out of these chains.

257
00:15:08,417 --> 00:15:09,377
You got it.

258
00:15:09,757 --> 00:15:12,097
Psychic powers, don't fail me now.

259
00:15:12,437 --> 00:15:13,557
Chains come off.

260
00:15:13,817 --> 00:15:14,937
Chains come off.

261
00:15:15,137 --> 00:15:16,497
Your links are getting looser.

262
00:15:16,777 --> 00:15:18,157
The metal's getting weaker.

263
00:15:18,677 --> 00:15:19,977
Chains be gone.

264
00:15:21,497 --> 00:15:22,137
Nothing.

265
00:15:22,977 --> 00:15:24,237
Well, we're stuck.

266
00:15:24,537 --> 00:15:25,497
Nice knowing you guys.

267
00:15:25,557 --> 00:15:26,997
I still can't stop laughing.

268
00:15:27,717 --> 00:15:30,417
Did you see the look on those fishmen's faces when I stood up?

269
00:15:31,017 --> 00:15:31,537
Priceless.

270
00:15:31,537 --> 00:15:41,977
He's not moving.

271
00:15:42,317 --> 00:15:43,077
Is he dead?

272
00:15:43,257 --> 00:15:45,357
Just keep still and they won't know.

273
00:15:47,917 --> 00:15:51,037
What about this old skeleton hanging off the ledge?

274
00:15:51,457 --> 00:15:53,277
How did something like that even get here?

275
00:15:53,657 --> 00:15:54,457
Who knows?

276
00:15:54,597 --> 00:15:55,477
Sure is weird.

277
00:15:55,477 --> 00:15:59,257
Maybe it got swept up in the current when Captain Horty busted through the wall.

278
00:15:59,377 --> 00:16:00,837
Let's pull it up on the bridge.

279
00:16:00,837 --> 00:16:01,897
Perfect.

280
00:16:03,157 --> 00:16:05,657
Brook can free us later if he keeps pretending to be dead.

281
00:16:05,997 --> 00:16:08,357
Who knew being a skeleton would come in so handy?

282
00:16:08,977 --> 00:16:11,137
Poor guy was probably adrift at sea.

283
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:13,297
I can't help but feel sorry for him.

284
00:16:13,297 --> 00:16:15,437
It looks like he died a long time ago.

285
00:16:15,837 --> 00:16:16,477
Retire!

286
00:16:17,557 --> 00:16:17,717
Huh?

287
00:16:18,097 --> 00:16:18,457
Ah!

288
00:16:19,517 --> 00:16:21,117
I did die.

289
00:16:21,517 --> 00:16:22,577
He's alive!

290
00:16:23,577 --> 00:16:24,017
Somewhat.

291
00:16:24,177 --> 00:16:25,817
Well, I may do at least.

292
00:16:25,937 --> 00:16:26,797
The name's Brook.

293
00:16:26,797 --> 00:16:37,117
Nice one, Brook.

294
00:16:41,117 --> 00:16:45,537
You want to touch my Avro?

295
00:16:45,777 --> 00:16:46,697
And rub him!

296
00:16:46,697 --> 00:16:49,177
Why don't you rub it and make a wish?

297
00:16:49,177 --> 00:16:50,177
Enough!

298
00:16:50,177 --> 00:16:50,677
Enough!

299
00:16:59,237 --> 00:17:00,457
So much for that.

300
00:17:05,137 --> 00:17:07,837
If I laugh any harder, I'll die!

301
00:17:07,837 --> 00:17:09,377
We're all gonna die!

302
00:17:09,677 --> 00:17:11,857
We wouldn't have gotten caught if it weren't for you!

303
00:17:11,997 --> 00:17:12,757
Please help!

304
00:17:12,897 --> 00:17:13,957
They're killing me!

305
00:17:14,337 --> 00:17:15,417
Wait, never mind.

306
00:17:15,717 --> 00:17:17,257
You're killing me too!

307
00:17:18,817 --> 00:17:21,337
Well, at least Nami and the others escaped.

308
00:17:22,197 --> 00:17:25,317
Soon, Luffy and the rest of the crew will come get us out of here.

309
00:17:25,397 --> 00:17:26,077
Wishful thinking!

310
00:17:26,297 --> 00:17:27,237
What if they don't?

311
00:17:27,837 --> 00:17:28,817
As Robin would say,

312
00:17:28,817 --> 00:17:33,597
Oh, I hope Nami hasn't been eaten by some deep-sea creature.

313
00:17:34,877 --> 00:17:36,217
Just like her!

314
00:17:50,817 --> 00:17:53,077
This poneglyph is different from the others.

315
00:17:53,617 --> 00:17:54,757
Now, let's see.

316
00:17:55,997 --> 00:17:57,757
It looks like a letter.

317
00:17:57,757 --> 00:17:59,897
As well as an apology.

318
00:18:01,397 --> 00:18:03,237
But who is this apology for?

319
00:18:03,957 --> 00:18:05,637
And why did you engrave it in stone?

320
00:18:07,257 --> 00:18:07,957
Joy Boy.

321
00:18:27,757 --> 00:18:36,217
That's a lot of money!

322
00:18:36,557 --> 00:18:37,537
$400 million?

323
00:18:37,777 --> 00:18:39,177
When did that go up, huh?

324
00:18:39,557 --> 00:18:41,457
No one cares about your bounty!

325
00:18:41,457 --> 00:18:46,197
Obviously, they're using the others as bait.

326
00:18:46,257 --> 00:18:47,117
Think about it, Luffy.

327
00:18:47,457 --> 00:18:48,517
You're infamous now.

328
00:18:48,717 --> 00:18:50,837
The conflict at Marine Ford made sure of that.

329
00:18:51,777 --> 00:18:53,577
Once you surpass $300 million,

330
00:18:53,837 --> 00:18:55,397
it rarely increases again.

331
00:18:59,737 --> 00:19:00,657
Well, anyway,

332
00:19:01,097 --> 00:19:02,657
if someone wants to fight me,

333
00:19:02,657 --> 00:19:03,257
I'll fight him!

334
00:19:03,257 --> 00:19:04,017
I beg you,

335
00:19:04,117 --> 00:19:05,257
don't act rashly!

336
00:19:07,257 --> 00:19:08,457
They have father.

337
00:19:13,157 --> 00:19:14,857
My father needs me!

338
00:19:15,357 --> 00:19:16,397
I have to help!

339
00:19:16,577 --> 00:19:17,677
I'm coming, Daddy!

340
00:19:19,937 --> 00:19:20,237
Megalo!

341
00:19:20,237 --> 00:19:26,577
I can't just stay here!

342
00:19:26,637 --> 00:19:27,217
Come back!

343
00:19:27,437 --> 00:19:28,077
Shira Hoshi!

344
00:19:28,777 --> 00:19:30,757
Megalo!

345
00:19:31,097 --> 00:19:31,737
Don't move!

346
00:19:32,317 --> 00:19:33,777
You could die!

347
00:19:34,777 --> 00:19:36,757
If I don't save father,

348
00:19:37,317 --> 00:19:37,877
then he...

349
00:19:37,877 --> 00:19:40,037
I do understand the urgency.

350
00:19:40,437 --> 00:19:41,117
But please,

351
00:19:41,297 --> 00:19:42,257
you must listen!

352
00:19:42,737 --> 00:19:43,537
You...

353
00:19:43,537 --> 00:19:45,017
He's right.

354
00:19:45,237 --> 00:19:46,997
You can't go back right now.

355
00:19:47,717 --> 00:19:48,337
You too?

356
00:19:49,157 --> 00:19:50,417
The one person

357
00:19:50,417 --> 00:19:52,037
that Horty is most afraid of

358
00:19:52,037 --> 00:19:53,217
in the Ryugu Kingdom

359
00:19:53,217 --> 00:19:55,617
is you, Princess.

360
00:19:56,317 --> 00:19:56,957
Your power.

361
00:19:59,097 --> 00:20:01,317
Even if Horty does change the island

362
00:20:01,317 --> 00:20:02,337
to suit his needs,

363
00:20:02,457 --> 00:20:03,617
you'll still be a threat.

364
00:20:04,377 --> 00:20:05,777
If you summon the Sea Kings,

365
00:20:06,177 --> 00:20:07,857
everything will come crashing down

366
00:20:07,857 --> 00:20:08,537
in an instant.

367
00:20:09,637 --> 00:20:10,537
That's why he took

368
00:20:10,537 --> 00:20:11,677
King Neptune hostage,

369
00:20:12,037 --> 00:20:13,397
to neutralize the princess

370
00:20:13,397 --> 00:20:14,717
and to lure her back.

371
00:20:14,837 --> 00:20:16,377
You're saying this whole time,

372
00:20:16,937 --> 00:20:18,977
they've really been after Shira Hoshi.

373
00:20:19,377 --> 00:20:19,817
You.

374
00:20:20,537 --> 00:20:21,717
Yes, but not in the way

375
00:20:21,717 --> 00:20:22,537
you might think.

376
00:20:22,977 --> 00:20:24,257
Horty doesn't want to capture

377
00:20:24,257 --> 00:20:25,757
the princess to use her power.

378
00:20:26,377 --> 00:20:27,537
This may sound cruel,

379
00:20:27,677 --> 00:20:29,157
but he'd prefer a threat like her

380
00:20:29,157 --> 00:20:30,317
not exist at all.

381
00:20:31,097 --> 00:20:31,917
That's why he partnered

382
00:20:31,917 --> 00:20:32,857
with Vander Decken.

383
00:20:33,517 --> 00:20:35,257
Decken is capable of killing her.

384
00:20:35,537 --> 00:20:36,317
Plain and simple.

385
00:20:36,857 --> 00:20:37,817
He'll destroy anything

386
00:20:37,817 --> 00:20:39,057
that stands in his way.

387
00:20:39,457 --> 00:20:39,857
Hmm.

388
00:20:40,537 --> 00:20:41,297
That's right.

389
00:20:41,777 --> 00:20:42,817
Horty wants the princess

390
00:20:42,817 --> 00:20:44,217
to rush into the plaza.

391
00:20:44,677 --> 00:20:44,977
There,

392
00:20:45,457 --> 00:20:46,797
she would be most vulnerable.

393
00:20:47,197 --> 00:20:47,477
Um,

394
00:20:47,557 --> 00:20:49,117
my family has mentioned

395
00:20:49,117 --> 00:20:50,037
my power before,

396
00:20:50,157 --> 00:20:51,257
but I'm afraid that's all.

397
00:20:51,597 --> 00:20:52,857
Even if you were to ask me

398
00:20:52,857 --> 00:20:54,277
to communicate with the Sea Kings,

399
00:20:54,357 --> 00:20:55,537
I don't think I could do it.

400
00:20:55,657 --> 00:20:56,217
Not now.

401
00:20:56,557 --> 00:20:57,297
To be honest,

402
00:20:57,677 --> 00:20:58,477
I'm not convinced

403
00:20:58,477 --> 00:20:59,437
that I have the power

404
00:20:59,437 --> 00:21:00,437
in the first place.

405
00:21:01,057 --> 00:21:02,417
Whether you do or not,

406
00:21:02,417 --> 00:21:03,757
Horty has no qualms

407
00:21:03,757 --> 00:21:04,437
with killing you

408
00:21:04,437 --> 00:21:05,457
just to be safe.

409
00:21:06,897 --> 00:21:07,377
Therefore,

410
00:21:07,717 --> 00:21:09,317
we must not let him find out

411
00:21:09,317 --> 00:21:10,077
that you aren't able

412
00:21:10,077 --> 00:21:11,117
to control the power.

413
00:21:11,657 --> 00:21:12,977
The more afraid of you he is,

414
00:21:13,037 --> 00:21:14,437
the better things are for us.

415
00:21:14,617 --> 00:21:15,177
All right.

416
00:21:15,357 --> 00:21:15,957
Are you done?

417
00:21:16,317 --> 00:21:16,637
Good.

418
00:21:17,037 --> 00:21:18,017
Then I'm going.

419
00:21:19,017 --> 00:21:19,777
Hey, Shark,

420
00:21:20,017 --> 00:21:21,377
take me back to the palace.

421
00:21:21,697 --> 00:21:21,957
Ja.

422
00:21:22,217 --> 00:21:24,077
I'm leaving the crybaby with you.

423
00:21:24,337 --> 00:21:24,877
That cool?

424
00:21:25,577 --> 00:21:26,337
Hell yeah.

425
00:21:26,717 --> 00:21:27,037
Luffy,

426
00:21:27,357 --> 00:21:28,377
I told you to wait.

427
00:21:29,137 --> 00:21:29,337
Huh?

428
00:21:29,777 --> 00:21:30,897
You don't get it.

429
00:21:31,037 --> 00:21:32,277
You people have no business

430
00:21:32,277 --> 00:21:33,117
fighting Horty.

431
00:21:33,257 --> 00:21:34,597
What's the big deal, huh?

432
00:21:35,157 --> 00:21:36,077
We can't fight

433
00:21:36,077 --> 00:21:36,837
because we're humans,

434
00:21:36,917 --> 00:21:37,577
is that it?

435
00:21:37,617 --> 00:21:38,517
It doesn't make sense

436
00:21:38,517 --> 00:21:39,497
when you two say it.

437
00:21:39,537 --> 00:21:40,757
Quit complicating things.

438
00:21:40,937 --> 00:21:41,597
That's right.

439
00:21:41,817 --> 00:21:43,277
This battle isn't for you.

440
00:21:43,777 --> 00:21:44,497
If you win,

441
00:21:44,557 --> 00:21:45,557
the surviving fishmen

442
00:21:45,557 --> 00:21:47,117
will go on hating humans again.

443
00:21:51,697 --> 00:21:52,257
Please,

444
00:21:52,257 --> 00:21:53,857
allow me to handle it.

445
00:21:54,377 --> 00:21:55,337
I can't.

446
00:21:55,337 --> 00:21:57,257
Not when my crew is in trouble.

447
00:21:57,957 --> 00:21:59,437
It's not that I don't trust you,

448
00:21:59,597 --> 00:22:01,497
but this fight is personal for me, too.

449
00:22:02,397 --> 00:22:03,357
You guys.

450
00:22:04,037 --> 00:22:05,157
They're both right.

451
00:22:09,037 --> 00:22:10,317
Stay out of this.

452
00:22:10,537 --> 00:22:11,097
Wait here.

453
00:22:11,377 --> 00:22:12,357
Not a chance.

454
00:22:12,757 --> 00:22:14,277
Such a stubborn fool.

455
00:22:14,377 --> 00:22:15,477
Just shut up already.

456
00:22:16,197 --> 00:22:17,297
I said I'm going.

457
00:22:17,777 --> 00:22:19,037
Stop me if you can.

458
00:22:19,997 --> 00:22:20,477
Luffy.

459
00:22:25,337 --> 00:22:28,017
Since we were allies before,

460
00:22:28,297 --> 00:22:30,557
I had hoped that you would honor my request.

461
00:22:31,177 --> 00:22:33,317
How easily I forget who you are.

462
00:22:34,017 --> 00:22:36,477
Hard-headedness truly does run in your family.

463
00:22:37,697 --> 00:22:39,297
If you're not going to listen to me,

464
00:22:39,637 --> 00:22:40,997
I have no choice.

465
00:22:40,997 --> 00:22:58,457
Stand down, Luffy.

466
00:23:01,457 --> 00:23:02,317
Or else.

467
00:23:02,317 --> 00:23:10,757
Fearing that the Straw Hats' interference

468
00:23:10,757 --> 00:23:12,277
may do more harm than good,

469
00:23:12,537 --> 00:23:13,997
a battle of wills breaks up

470
00:23:13,997 --> 00:23:15,337
between Luffy and Jinbei.

471
00:23:15,757 --> 00:23:17,457
While the two friends go head-to-head,

472
00:23:17,877 --> 00:23:20,117
Hordi's underlings wreak havoc in the city.

473
00:23:20,797 --> 00:23:22,477
Still captured at Ryugu Palace,

474
00:23:22,797 --> 00:23:23,917
the rest of the Straw Hats

475
00:23:23,917 --> 00:23:26,257
launch a very peculiar escape plan.

476
00:23:26,857 --> 00:23:28,277
On the next One Piece,

477
00:23:28,277 --> 00:23:29,877
a rift opens up.

478
00:23:30,117 --> 00:23:31,517
Luffy versus Jinbei.

479
00:23:31,897 --> 00:23:33,637
I'm going to be king of the pirates!

